The change fixes both causes. `RenewSubscription` claims a period under the store lock, so only one caller creates and charges the invoice. The period moves even when the charge fails, and `RenewDue` keeps going and joins the errors. The tests cover concurrent renewals, an outage followed by a second run, and one failure not stopping the others.

One optional note, not a reason to revise: the cancel-at-period-end branch in `subscriptions.go:178-187` is not claimed. Two concurrent runs can both cancel the same subscription and both count it, so `RenewDue`'s returned count can be too high. No invoice or charge is involved, and no requirement covers the count under concurrency.

